1 OCCU Fänrik, Skalmejblåsare, Hautboisten (army piper)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jonas Löfving was enlisted to Jönköpings regemente as a volunteer on 1 July 1720 in Stockholm. He was then upgraded to förare in 1721 and apparently to fänrik upon his retirement from the army, which was because th
2 CONC e holder of his position returned from being a war prisoner in Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT It cannot be correct that he was new in the military. His age fits with skalmejeblåsare Jonas Löfving. He rejoined the military to become an officer, maybe to be able to marry his aristocratic wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/A0028346_00339#?c=&amp;m=&am
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Generalmönsterrulla 1719, Jönköpings regemente Staben: Hautboisten Jonas Löfving, avgången från regementet i Juni 1719 Sid 10
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas followed his farther Per in the office of a skjalmeblåsare (musician) in Jönköping's regemente. Jonas was "hautboisten" when the regiment surrendered in Stralsund in 1715 and was kept as prisoner in Preussia. He returned in 
2 CONC 1716. He is on the record of the regiment still in June 1719, together with Johan Löfving and Hans Löfving - also "hautboisten", probably his brothers - but retired then.   
