1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mikael Wejdling var borgmästare i Skänninge.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Födelse:	8 feb 1749 - Linköping Östergötlands län
2 CONT * Död:	13 feb 1820 - Skänninge, Östergötland, Sverige
2 CONT * Föräldrar:	Alexander Wejdling, Hedvig Christina Wejdling (född Höppener)
2 CONT * Syskon:	Hedvig Elisabeth Grönberg (född Wejdling), Okänd, Okänd, Anna Margaretha Roxén (född Wejdling), Okänd, Johan Adolf Alexandersson Wejdling, Okänd, Ulrica Charlotta Jöransson (född Wejdling), Okänd, Christina Dorothea Wejd
2 CONC ling
2 CONT * Maka:	Elisabeth Margaretha Wejdling (född Livin)
2 CONT * Maka:	Okänd Weidling
2 CONT * Maka:	Margareta Weidling (född Hammar)
2 CONT * Barn:	Catharina Elisabeth Wollfelt (född Weidling), Okänd, Claes Michaël Wejdling, Claes Michaël Wejdling, Carl Otto Fredrik Wejdling, Okänd, Gustaf Alexander Wejdling, Okänd
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Michael at first was  a Rådman  then went on to be a Borgmästare of the area.
2 CONT
2 CONT A "rådman" was a member of a city or town council, mostly referred to as magistrate ("magistrat"). The "rådman" was elected among the town/city burghers, i.e. master craftsmen, important (and wealthy) merchants etc. Minor shop-kee
2 CONC pers, journeymen, servants, labourers etc. were not burghers and couldn't vote (and couldn't be elected).
2 CONT From among the eligible burghers three men were proposed as "borgmästare", mayor, and the King appointed one of the suggested men. The mayor was the chairman of the town/city council and would commonly have served a number of year
2 CONC s on the council before rising to mayor.
2 CONT The magistrates had two functions:
2 CONT 1. they ran the town/city ("city hall")
2 CONT 2. they served as the town/city court (of appeal), "rådhusrätt" (old Swedish, "rådstuvurätt")
2 CONT In the country the primary court was the "häradsrätt", in towns and cities the primary court was until 1849 the "kämnärsrätt". The decisions of a "kämnärsrätt" could be appealed to the "rådhusrätt". In 1849 the "kämnärsrätt" was a
2 CONC bolished and the primary court of towns/cities was the "rådhusrätt". This system held good until 1972 when both "häradsrätt" and "rådhusrätt" were transformed into "tingsrätt", finally after nearly 600 years abolishing the last re
2 CONC mains of difference between town and country.
2 CONT So, being a counsellor or mayor in the early 1800's meant not only that you held a high position, it also meant that you were highly successful in your business (you couldn't be a "career counsellor").
