1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT In 1802 the Carl "reste till Upsala academie", which means that he went to attend the university at Uppsala. Uppsala university was founded in 1477 and is the oldest university in the Nordic countries. However, it wasn't a very go
2 CONC od university. If you wanted a top-notch education for your son, you sent him to Germany. This has of course changed since then and Uppsala now ranks among the 100 best universities in the world. But in 1802 - no.
2 CONT Having been to university was in no way needed for running even the biggest business - in fact, it could be detrimental. At univeristy you learned nothing of use for business, like arithmetic or languages and certainly not busines
2 CONC s administration. Specializing in law could possibly be useful, but most men trained in law would go to the higher courts, the courts of appeal, and also to the higher administration in Stockholm. Going to university was instead a
2 CONC n excellent way of advancing socially; there were four estates, the lowest being the farmers, then burghers, then the clergy and on top the nobility (until 1866). So, studying to become a vicar - eventually perhaps a bishop (thoug
2 CONC h that WOULD take studies in Germany) - was a leap upward, from the burgher's estate to the clergy's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime before 1810 Carl came back to follow in his fathers footsteps and was a mayor for more than 55 years, before 1810 until his death  in 1865.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his housekeeper, Maria, had 8 illigitimate children, from 1819-1836, then he married her in 1837.
