1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anna, död 1677 och begraven 1686-01-15 i Göteborg. Gift med översten för Närkes och Värmlands regemente Johan Gordon, född 1617 (1607?) i febr. i Aberdeen i Skottland, död 1653-01-27 i Stockholm och begraven i Sköl
2 CONC lersta kyrka, där hans epitafium uppsattes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMSON, ANNA [SSNE 5442]
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname
2 CONT     THOMSON, GORDON, MACLEAN, MACKLIER First name
2 CONT     ANNA Title/rank Nationality
2 CONT     SCOT Region
2 CONT     GOTHENBURG Social status Education Religion
2 CONT
2 CONT Text source Anna Thomson was the daughter of Colonel Thomas Thomson [SSNE 1648] and his wife Catherine Murray. Anna married Colonel John Gordon [SSNE 2515], who died in 1653. She then married John Maclean, 1st Baronet [SSNE 1631] 
2 CONC in his third marriage around 1659. Anna died after suffering a chest and arm infection and was buried on 15 January 1686 in Gothenburg along with her husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  G. Elgenstierna, Svenska Adelns Attartavlor, vol. v, p.142 and vol. 8, p.265; J.N.M. Maclean, The Macleans of Sweden (Edinburgh, 1971), pp. 26 and 28; W. Berg, Samlingar till Göteborgs Historia Christina Kyrkas böcker,(Gothenburg
2 CONC , 1890), vol.1, p.519. Female. Service record
2 CONT
2 CONT SWEDEN, GOTHENBURG
2 CONT     Arrived 1653-01-01
2 CONT     Departed 1686-01-15
2 CONT     Purpose MISC
