1 NOTE {geni:about_me} wILLIAM 2 FWB 2010:
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.	Felix Mårten Gabriel Wessman-2 (Fredrik Mårten-1) was born on 04 Mar 1867 in Wesstomta, Larum, Hannäs Parish, Östergötlands län, Småland region, Sweden. He died on 18 Feb 1897 in Marathon, Poland Twp., Buena Vista Co., Iowa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Felix Mårten Gabriel Wessman: General Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Felix emigrated together with his parents in 1882, May 24. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness to Felix's and Dora's marriage was H.J. Leyson (sp?). Ceremony performed by Bennett Mitchell. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thursday, 4 March 1897 Storm Lake Vidette
2 CONT
2 CONT Felix WESSMAN was born in Sweden on March 24th and died in Marathon February 18, 1897. He was married July 31, 1889 to Miss Dora MAGGS. He leaves a widow and 4 children-3 sons and 1 daughter, a mother also, and 2 brothers and 3 si
2 CONC sters to mourn the loss of a loved one. Mr.
2 CONT
2 CONT WESSMAN was well known in this community and respected by all. During the meetings held recently he took a decided stand for Christ and gave himself to God, and his name to the church. During the short time that elapsed between un
2 CONC iting with the church and his death, he gave evidence that he was in earnest. During his sickness he expressed his great confidence in the ability of Christ to save. He said, “I used to think that there would be time enough to rep
2 CONC ent and prepare for death when the last sickness came, but I now know differently; this would no time to prepare.” When asked by a friend if all was well he responded “All is well Glory to Jesus”, and then sung part of a familiar 
2 CONC hymn. He said to his wife, “I hear the harps.” After a spell of semi-unconsciousness he said to Sister WESSMAN, “Have you come so soon?” and asked the question, “Which world are we in?” apparently thinking he had entered into the 
2 CONC glory and trust the redeemer of this world, thus verifying the Word in describing certain characters which says “The end of that man is peace.” The funeral was held at the M. E. Church on Saturday afternoon, and was largely attend
2 CONC ed. The pall bearers were C. J. PARKER, C. P. CORNEILIUSSEN, C. E. CAMERON, E. LARSON, P. MORRISSEY, and O. J. JOHNSON. The interment took place at the Alta Cemetery. (Alta Advertiser)
2 CONT
2 CONT Contacts for the Alta Iowa Cemeteries:
2 CONT
2 CONT Russ Post712-284-2110
2 CONT
2 CONT Dave Mortenson712-284-1393
2 CONT
2 CONT Jim712-200-2530
2 CONT
2 CONT Dora Jane Maggs daughter of John Stewart Maggs and Jane Parrott[50] was born on 15 Dec 1861 in Winterset, Center Twp., Madison Co., Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Felix Mårten Gabriel Wessman and Dora Jane Maggs were married on 31 Jul 1889 in Alta, Buena Vista Co., Iowa[18]. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	Earl Leroy Wessman was born on 15 Oct 1892 in Alta, Nokomis Twp., Buena Vista Co., Iowa. He married Margaret B. Zeigler on 13 Jun 1918 in Sioux Falls, Minnehaha Co., South Dakota. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 25.	ii. Clarence Leslie Wessman[51] was born on 28 May 1890 in Alta, Nokomis Twp., Buena Vista[52]. He married Clara V. Ross on 09 Oct 1912 in Alta, Nokomis Twp., Buena Vista[53]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.	Clifford Guy Wessman[51] was born on 31 Jan 1894 in Alta, Nokomis Twp., Buena Vista. He married Ida May Preston on 28 Feb 1917 in Alta, Nokomis Twp., Buena Vista Co., Iowa[54]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Clifford Guy Wessman: General Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marr. Aff Dvt signed by C.D. Peterson. Ceremony performed by FB Nixon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Vera Fern Wessman[51] was born in Mar 1895 in Alta, Nokomis Twp., Buena Vista. She married Carl David Florentine Peterson on 26 Jan 1916 in Alta, Nokomis Twp., Buena Vista Co., Iowa[55]. She died in Santa Ana, California. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill 2-2-2010:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Sarah K. Wessman s dödsruna också att från och med 1903 hade hon 8 barn varav 5 levde och 2 var i Sverige. Från vad jag vet, 3 för dem som bor och i USA var Hedwig Anderson, Claus och Axel. Av de 3 som dog Felix, vet jag dog i 
2 CONC USA omkring 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++ +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
2 CONT
2 CONT Chris Younggreen 1884/85-1907
2 CONT
2 CONT Svar: 9
2 CONT
2 CONT Re: augusti Younggren - Laurens, Pocahontas, Iowa 1895
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Younggreen Sullivan (Visa inlägg) Inlagd: 18 januari 2005 1:19
2 CONT
2 CONT Ämne: Query
2 CONT
2 CONT Efternamn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tyvärr, vet jag inget Oss Mellan Familjen i augusti Younggreen (Younggren) och Carl A. Peterson eller Sarah Wilhelmina Wessman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kanske de bara var grannar eller vänner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jag kollade 1895 Iowa folkräkningen i den regionen i Iowa och hittade
2 CONT
2 CONT Felix Wessman f. ABT 1867 Sverige i den närbelägna staden Marathon, Polen Township, Buena Vista County, IA
2 CONT
2 CONT och
2 CONT
2 CONT Claus Wessman f. ABT 1861 sverige på Landsbygden Polen Township, Buena Vista County, IA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kunde de ha Varit yngre bröder i din Sarah Wessman?
2 CONT
2 CONT Ur Laurens, Iowa historia jag har
2 CONT
2 CONT Claus Wessman gåva Mollie (Amelia?) Kimball.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claus Wessman hade en sele butik i Laurens 1905-1915.
