1 NOTE {geni:about_me} <blockquote>'''LIEUTENANT COLONEL DAVID SINCLAIR OF FINNEKUMLA'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''David Sinclair, second son of Seba by Barbe Halcro, also established himself in Sweden, where he was naturalised and admitted to the [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sinclair_nr_626 House of Nobles] under the n
2 CONC umber 626, in the year 1655. He was Colonel of a Regiment of Cavalry, and married Katherine, daughter of John Maclean, Seigneur de Gasvadholm and Hagby. This David Sinclair was slain at the battle of Warsaw, in Poland, in 1656, le
2 CONC aving:  (1) William Sinclair, his heir (2) Anne de Sinclair, married to Colonel the Baron de Kruse. After Colonel Sinclair's death his relict married Major-General Hamilton. [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/
2 CONC 318/mode/1up The Saint-Clairs of the Isles, p. 318]'' </blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lieutenant Colonel David Sinclair is the son of William Sinclair of Saba. His uncle James, Lord Eythin, in his last will and testament dated 10 April 1651, left him two thousand four hundred Reixdollars: "which I am adebted to 
2 CONC him by Vertue of obligations I have given him, but also to have and resave money or satisfaction in lands and otherwayes for the soume of twa thousand fyve hundreth Reixdollars, the which I lent to his father and my brother Willia
2 CONC m Sinckler of Seaby as a token of my love for him." [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/230/mode/1up The Last Will and Testament of James, Lord Eythin]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Last Will and Testament of James, Lord Eythin===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/229/mode/1up Page First]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/230/mode/1up Page Second]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/231/mode/1up Page Third]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lieutenant Colonel David Sinclair was killed in action on 19 July 1656, during the seige of Warsaw. Th. A. Fischer said this of him: "David Sinclair, who came to Sweden in 1651, was Colonel of a cavalry-regiment, and shot by a 
2 CONC cannon-ball in sight of the King at the Battle of Warsaw in 1656." [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/132/mode/1up The Scots in Sweden, p. 132]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Marriage of David Sinclair and Catharina Macklier (aka Katherine Maclean, daughter of John Maclean, Seigneur de Gasvadholm and Hagby)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Catharina. Född 1631. Gift 1) 14.12.1651 med överste David Sinclair, adlad Sinclair av Finnekumla (död i strid 1 8.7.1656, Warszawa), son till William Sinclair och hans hustru Barbara Halcro. 2) 1661 med generalmajor Malcolm Ha
2 CONC milton, Baron Hamilton till Hageby (död 1698), son till Kapten John Hamilton  till Tullyreny, Co Fermanagh, och hans hustru Jean Somerville. Hon begr. 8.8.1709 i Göteborg. Barn i båda äktenskapen. [http://www.gbgtomter.se/Rote_5/5
2 CONC .60.pdf Tomt 60 - Göteborgs tomtägare 1637-1807]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Sinclair/6000000004350410970?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1526761104604&through=6000000004289437678
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/N-N-Sinclair/6000000071134556835?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1526760908959&through=6000000071134556835
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Sinclair/6000000007334156256?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1526761174672&through=6000000004289437678
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Adelsvapen===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sinclair_nr_626 '''David Sinclair'''], naturaliserad '''Sinclair, till Finnekumla''' i [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnekumla_socken Finnekumla socken], Älvsborgs län. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kom 1631 till''' Sverige (jämte sin äldre broder John, som blev major vid Hepburns gröna brigad 1631 och överstelöjtnant 1632 samt stupade under trettioåriga kriget). Var överstelöjtnant 1650. Överste för ett värvat rytterirege
2 CONC mente 1655 på våren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Naturaliserad svensk''' adelsman 1655-06-01 (introducerad 1655 under n:o 626). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sårad av en kanonkula''' i [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bel%C3%A4gringen_av_Warszawa_(1656 slaget vid Warschau] 1656-07-18 i spetsen för en skvadron av regementet och död 1656-07-19. 
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>
2 CONT  "Han köpte för de penningar, som hans fader förmått skicka honom och sedan allt hopp för honom var ute att kunna få återkomma till Skottland, säteriet Finnekumla, vilket dock sedermera reducerades från sonen, fick vid naturalisat
2 CONC ionen som svensk adelsman behålla sitt urgamla vapen med tillägg av en vit, fembladig ros mitt i korset till betecknande av att han tillhörde kungl. partiet i Skottland, som bar vita kokarder. medan däremot Cromwells hade röda." <
2 CONC /blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1651-12-14''' i Kristine församling i Göteborg med Catharina [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Makel%C3%A9er_nr_513 Makeléer] i hennes 1:a gifte (gift 2:o 1661 med generalmajoren och landshövdingen Malkolm Hamilton, fr
2 CONC iherre [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Hamilton_af_Hageby_nr_99#TAB_2 Hamilton al Hageby], född 1635, död 1698), född 1637, död 1709 och begraven 1709-08-08 i Göteborg, men först 1717-02-23 nedsatt i familjegraven i Kristine
2 CONC  kyrka i Göteborg, dotter av kommissarien '''Johan (eller Hans) Maclean''', adlad '''Makeléer''', och hans 1:a fru '''Anna Gubbertz'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical and Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/saintclairsofisl00sain#page/139/mode/1up/search/barbara+halcro The Saint Clairs of the Isles, pp. 139-141 for the Sinclairs of Tohop and Saba]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotsinsweden00fisc#page/n10/mode/1up Th. A. Fischer, The Scots in Sweden (Otto Shulze, Edinburgh, 1907),  278 pp. including index]
