1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===================================================================================
2 CONT Anna Catharina Cronman III married Hans Christoffer von Rohr (1626-1700). Please do not merge her with her sister of the same name. Please do not merge her with her aunt of the same name. If you have questions please see the canon
2 CONC ical genealogy by Gustaf Magnus Elgenstierna (1871-1948). Gabriel Anrep (1821-1907) confused Anna Catharina Cronman I and Anna Catharina Cronman III and this was corrected by Gustaf Magnus Elgenstierna (1871-1948) in 1923.
2 CONT ===================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Catharina Cronman III (c1660-1685)
2 CONT (b. circa 1660, Sweden - d. December 03, 1685, Angered, Alvsborg, Sweden) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT Joachim Cronman (1638-1703) and Lunetta Makeléer (1639-1693).
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Anna Catharina Cronman II who died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: She appears to have married Hans Christoffer von Rohr (1626-1700) around 1677. If she was born in 1660 she would have been 17 at the time her fist child was born. If this is the correct Anna Catharina Cronman III was 30 
2 CONC years younger than the father of her children
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Joachim Von Rohr (1677-1757) who was a lieutenant colonel in the Swedish Army and the commander of the Dalarö fortress and he married Catharina Charlotta Klingenberg (1680-1758) on February 04, 1699 in Sweden; Maria Eliz
2 CONC abeth von Rohr (1679-1710) who died during the plague epidemic at age 29; Sofia Anna von Rohr (1680-1686) who died as a youth; Anna Catharina von Rohr (1682-1715); Hans Christoffer Von Rohr II (1684-1754) who married Helena Cathar
2 CONC ina von Spandekow (1691-1748) on August 10, 1711 in Klinov, Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship: Anna Catharina Cronman (c1658-1685) was the eighth great-grandmother of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Update: Corrected by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) on January 7, 2011 with the difference between Anna Catharina Cronman I and II and III. Gabriel Anrep incorrectly lists Anna Catharina Cronman (1620-?) as the wife of Hans Christ
2 CONC offer von Rohr I (1626–1700) because they are the same age. She would be the sister of Joachim Cronman but would have been almost 60 by time her first child was born. Gustaf Elgenstierna corrected the Anrep genealogy in the 1920s.
2 CONC  Anna Catharina Cronman (1660-?) III is now shown as the wife of Hans Christoffer von Rohr I (1626–1700). This makes the wife of von Rohr the daughter of Joachim Cronman. This which puts her at the proper age for bearing the child
2 CONC ren of von Rohr. This makes Von Rohr 30 years years older than Anna Catharina Cronman (1660-?), which is not unheard of. This error between the three Anna's of two generations has been repeated in many online genealogies. 
