2 CONT Text source
2 CONT
2 CONT James Thomson was a son of Thomas Thomson [SSNE 1648] and Catherine Murray. He served in the Swedish army from 1633 in his father's company. He cashiered himself sometime, probably in September, 1638, leaving with the rank of capt
2 CONC ain. Jacob Thomson probably fought at Wittstock in October 1636. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish Krigsarkiv, Muster Roll, 1633/6; 1634/2,5,18,23; 1635/1,9,20,24,25; 1636/1,17,18; 1637/3,7; 1638/4; C.O. Nordensvan, (ed.), Värmlands Regementes [Närkes och Värmlands Regementes] Historia: Andra Delen, Personal Historia (S
2 CONC tockholm, 1911), 38; G. Elgenstierna, Svenska Adelns Ättartavlor, vol. 8, pp.264-265. Service record
2 CONT
