1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Severin (Sören) was a famous academic who wrote in Latin, Greek and German apart from his native Danish. He was sent to school in Copenhagen when he was fourteen but he always called himself "Malmogius Scandus" - a
2 CONC  Scanian from Malmö. He later worked for the Danish army in Italy and occupied important positions in the Danish government.
